Day 31 - AWS EC2 Security Groups

Topics learned:

- Security Groups
- Inbound Rules
- Outbound Rules
- Common Ports
- Stateful Firewalls

What I learned:

- Security Groups protect EC2 instances.
- Inbound rules control incoming traffic.
- Outbound rules control outgoing traffic.
- SSH uses port 22.
- HTTP uses port 80.
- HTTPS uses port 443.
- Security Groups are stateful, meaning return traffic is automatically allowed.
